    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 020536\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n1036 PM PDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n*  Drier, cooler, and breezy conditions expected through the work \n   week.  \n\n*  Uncertainty increases this weekend with regards to tropical\n   moisture from Marie. \n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...Wednesday through Monday.\n\nDrier air will eliminate precipitation chances through Friday for \nmost locations as a trough deepens over the west coast and PWATs \nfall to half an inch or less. A few isolated storms may sneak into \nsouthern Mohave County on Thursday afternoon as moisture pushes \nthrough central Arizona. The trough will also support gusty \nsoutherly to southwesterly winds each afternoon, the strongest of \nwhich will peak between 30 and 40 mph across San Bernardino, Clark, \nMohave, and southern Nye counties. Expect highs in the 90s to low \n100s in valleys across the Mojave Desert. \n\nAttention turns to a potential moisture surge this weekend caused by \nthe influence of Tropical Storm Marie. Ensemble members are \ngravitating towards two solutions, one which would take the storm \nwest into the Pacific Ocean, and another which would bring the storm \nnorth towards California. Even if the low stays offshore, \nsouthwesterly flow may be able to pull a decent amount of moisture \ninland if the track is favorable. Models show PWATs increasing to \nthe 1.5 to 2.0 inch range along and south of Interstate 15 between \nSaturday and Monday. Precipitation chances will change based on the \npath of the system and high uncertainty remains at this time.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 06Z Forecast Package...There is \nreturning confidence in southwesterly gusts increasing in the Las \nVegas Valley around 08Z through 12-13Z, with gust speeds around 20 \nkts. Gusty southwest winds will return Wednesday mid-morning, with \ngust speeds between 25 and 30 kts. Gusts will decrease in speed and \nfrequency after sunset. FEW aoa 12 kft expected this evening. \nTemperatures remain below 100 degrees through the forecast period.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 06Z Forecast Package...Gusty south-\nsouthwesterly winds will return to the region Wednesday mid-morning \nwith speeds between 20 and 30 kts. The exception will be KDAG where \nwinds will gust from the west. No operationally significant cloud \ncover though the TAF period.\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Meltzer\nAVIATION...Soulat\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
